    <heading level="1">Verbal</heading>
    <exercise number="1" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>How can an exponential equation be solved?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Determine first if the equation can be rewritten so that each side uses the same base. If so, the exponents can be set equal to each other. If the equation cannot be rewritten so that each side uses the same base, then apply the logarithm to each side and use properties of logarithms to solve.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="2" has_solution="false">
